ols\" are different epistemic states, and the book is claiming both depending on which objection it's dodging.\n\nThe 3-sphere point still hasn't been addressed, three messages running now. That's not a \"beyond Newtonian tools\" case — it's standard differential geometry, checkable today, and it directly falsifies the specific line \"finite space requires an edge.\" I'd genuinely like to see how Theorem III's math appendix handles it, if it does at all — that's a concrete thing we can look at together rather than continuing to trade abstractions.",
